<div id="2026-11-06-kobra-start-print" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-06 — Kobra start-print from the queue</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Staff started a print from /3d/queue. The Kobra 3 (serial BECB-D68E-F519-16AB) had moved from 192.168.2.59 to 192.168.2.61; the farm row now stores that address. Start Print lists the files on the printer, searches them, and pre-selects a file when the item name and the file name share words.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> A dead address was treated as a slow printer, so the queue never searched. The file dialog then hid 248 files and only matched an exact model name, which the sprouting-lid job does not have. A stop also left the job at <code>printing</code> while the restart inserted a second row, so one green print showed twice in Active.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Stop and restart.</strong> Stop now puts the job back to <code>queued</code> with a "stopped on printer" note and marks the farm row idle. Starting the same file again on that printer resumes that row instead of inserting a twin; a different file still creates a new job. This is on disk in <code>PrinterLan.pm</code> and does not run until <code>:4003</code> is restarted.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Not done.</strong> The :4003 worker has not reloaded the .pm follow/enroll code, so the serial follow and stop-requeue/restart-resume are still disk-only. <code>printing_3d_jobs.labour_cost</code> and <code>cost_breakdown</code> now exist, so Complete and Cancel load; <code>labour_cost</code> declares <code>decimal(10,4)</code> to match the four-decimal writes in Costing/Traveler, but the column itself is still <code>decimal(10,0)</code> until the in-app schema-compare sync runs. Todo #2334 stays open. Todo #2666 stays paused.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Printing3d/Adapter/Anycubic.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Printing3d/LanMap.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/3d.pm</code>, <code>root/3d/queue.tt</code>, <code>script/printer_lan_sync.pl</code>, <code>root/Documentation/3d/Kobra3LanMode.tt</code>.</p>
</div>
